  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f424be585f9e04c79a96c8292e8b9db1, type: 3}
  m_Name: Troca_ConsorcioIntermunicipal
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Metis.Runtime::KnowledgeEntryData
  _title: "Cons\xF3rcio intermunicipal"
  _titleEn: Inter-municipal consortium
  _category: 2
  _unlockTrigger: 13
  _summary: "Cons\xF3rcio p\xFAblico \xE9 uma entidade criada por v\xE1rias cidades
    para fazer juntas o que sairia caro sozinho: comprar rem\xE9dios e m\xE1quinas,
    manter um hospital regional, tratar o lixo. Somar as compras d\xE1 poder de negocia\xE7\xE3o."
  _summaryEn: 'A public consortium is an entity created by several towns to do together
    what would be costly alone: buy medicine and machinery, run a regional hospital,
    treat waste. Pooling purchases gives bargaining power.'
  _realWorld: "A Lei 11.107/2005 regula os cons\xF3rcios p\xFAblicos no Brasil. Em
    Santa Catarina, o cons\xF3rcio CINCATARINA mant\xE9m uma central de compras compartilhadas
    para os munic\xEDpios associados, e a nova Lei de Licita\xE7\xF5es pede que cidades
    de at\xE9 10 mil habitantes prefiram esse caminho."
  _realWorldEn: Law 11,107/2005 governs public consortia in Brazil. In Santa Catarina,
    the CINCATARINA consortium runs a shared purchasing center for its member towns,
    and the new Public Procurement Law asks towns of up to 10,000 people to prefer
    this route.
  _tradeOffs: "Comprar junto barateia, mas cada decis\xE3o precisa de acordo entre
    prefeitos, e uma cidade sozinha perde liberdade de escolha."
  _tradeOffsEn: Buying together cuts costs, but every decision needs agreement among
    mayors, and a single town loses freedom of choice.
  _sources:
  - Label: "Lei 11.107/2005, cons\xF3rcios p\xFAblicos"
    Url: https://www.planalto.gov.br/ccivil_03/_ato2004-2006/2005/lei/l11107.htm
  - Label: "Lei 14.133/2021, Lei de Licita\xE7\xF5es"
    Url: https://www.planalto.gov.br/ccivil_03/_ato2019-2022/2021/lei/l14133.htm
